      "path": "prime-number-suite/generators/ose.c",
      "line": 53,
      "symbol": "malloc",
      "classification": "approved-invariant",
      "rationale": "checked_alloc is the sieve's single allocation boundary. It rejects zero-byte requests, verifies that malloc returned a non-null pointer, and terminates before a failed allocation can reach a caller. Call sites either prove their byte counts against SIZE_MAX or derive a nonzero rounded bit-buffer size from an already range-checked candidate count.",
      "invariant": "size is greater than zero on entry to malloc; every multiplication used to form size is checked against SIZE_MAX first; and the returned pointer is not exposed unless allocation is non-null.",
      "evidence": [
        "prime-number-suite/generators/ose.c::checked_alloc",
        "prime-number-suite/generators/ose.c::simple_sieve",
        "prime-number-suite/generators/ose.c::sieve_collect",
        "https://github.com/dlworrell/code-noodling/pull/8"
      ],
      "owner": "dlworrell",
      "reviewer": "dlworrell",
      "reviewed_at": "2026-08-08",
