      "path": "prime-number-suite/generators/ose.c",
      "line": 65,
      "symbol": "realloc",
      "classification": "approved-invariant",
      "rationale": "checked_realloc is used only to grow the result vector. vector_push checks capacity doubling and element-byte multiplication against SIZE_MAX before calling it. The wrapper stores realloc's result in a temporary pointer and exits on failure, so the caller's original allocation is never overwritten by a null result on any continuing path.",
      "invariant": "size is nonzero and overflow-checked; allocation receives realloc's return value before the caller's vector pointer is updated; and failure terminates while the original allocation remains valid until process teardown.",
      "evidence": [
        "prime-number-suite/generators/ose.c::checked_realloc",
        "prime-number-suite/generators/ose.c::vector_push",
        "https://github.com/dlworrell/code-noodling/pull/8"
      ],
